# Compendium token hygiene

When tool output, logs, JSON, or pasted blobs are large or noisy, call the MCP tool `compendium` with an `action` instead of dumping raw text into context.

Unknown action? Call `action: "catalog"` (or MCP `resources/list` on `cmp://skill/…`) then `action: "help"` with `id`.

## Quick map

| Situation | Call |
|-----------|------|
| ANSI / boilerplate / noisy logs | `action: "filter"` + `text` |
| git/cargo/npm/docker/kubectl stdout | `action: "compress_output"` + `text` |
| Untrusted text / possible secrets or IPI | `action: "sanitize"` + `text` (or `sanitize_input: true`) |
| Keep only lines about a question | `action: "filter_relevant"` or `filter` + `query` (BM25) |
| Rank chunks for a question | `action: "rerank"` + `query` + `items` / chunk `map` (hybrid if local embeddings up) |
| Why heuristic / LLM down? | `action: "llm_status"` (`force: true` for chat probe) |
| New sub-task / fresh agent turn | `action: "brief"` + `query` (+ optional `brief.root`); use returned structured briefing (Status/Evidence/Caveats/Sources/Read next) or `cache_key` as starter context |
| Dense rewrite of code/logs/JSON | `action: "compress"` + `text` (skip if &lt;~1000 chars unless `force`) |
| Long chat / transcript | `action: "prune_history"` (`strategy: "afm"` preferred) or `summarize` / `summarize_smart` |
| Huge file/corpus you may revisit | `action: "chunk"` then later `resolve` with `id` |
| Park bulky payload outside prompt | `action: "cache_store"` → keep only returned `key` |
| Guided recipe (logs, cargo fail, AFM, …) | `action: "playbooks"` then `playbook` + `id`, or read `cmp://skill/playbook/{id}` |
| Multi-file archive bundle | `action: "pack"` / `unpack` (size-capped; scripts never run) |
| Measure size / savings | `action: "count_tokens"` or `stats` |
| Discover actions | `action: "catalog"` / `help` (default compressed; `force: true` for full), or MCP resources `cmp://skill/index` |

## Rules of thumb

- If a single tool result is likely >~400 tokens of noise, run `filter` or `compress_output` first.
- Prefer `filter_relevant` when you already know the question the log must answer.
- Prefer `cache_store` over re-pasting the same large blob across turns (optional `COMPENDIUM_CACHE_DIR` for disk persistence).
- Prefer `chunk` index text over the full corpus; `resolve` only the ids you need.
- Prefer `catalog`/`help` (or resources) over guessing action fields; default `help` is compressed — use `force: true` for examples.
- Do not invent other tool names (`compendium_filter`, etc.) — there is only `compendium`.
- Response shape: `{ ok, action, result_json, error? }`. Parse `result_json` as JSON for the action payload.
- Smart actions report `backend: "local_llm" | "heuristic"`; heuristic fallback is normal when no local SLM URL is set.
